Subject: [PATCH 525/525] [DS4.1] PDL: from 16 rows the routed grouped GEMMs
 trigger after their K loop

The shared expert's SwiGLU, cast and down GEMM on the aux stream run in the SM
slots the routed gate/up GEMM's last CTAs free. Triggered at its start, the
gate/up GEMM lets the routed SwiGLU's CTAs launch into those slots and wait
there; the routed down GEMM, launched early in turn, holds every SM, and the
shared down GEMM runs after it, on the critical path (layer-chain traces on
GB10: it ends 14-16 us after the routed one at 16 and 48 rows, 4 us at 6 rows;
537-1208 us before it without PDL). At 6 rows that order pays: the gate/up
GEMM's last wave keeps DRAM to itself and ends 10-15 us earlier than with the
shared expert beside it. From 16 rows the shared down GEMM after the routed one
costs more than that.

From moe.LATE_TRIGGER_ROWS (16) rows the plan's grouped GEMMs begin with
pdl.wait() and call pdl.trigger() after the K loop
(grouped_fp8_fp4_gemm(trigger_after_loop=True): late_gate_up and late_down at
the decode tile height, and the prefill GEMMs), so the kernel after them
launches near their end and the shared expert runs beside the gate/up GEMM's
tail, as without PDL. Below 16 rows they keep pdl.chain(), the same kernels
as before.

